                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34fd0cc6-08cf-3aca-979e-611a2da30d80",
                                        "entry_id": "4aae96f7-fde4-3ba2-8df7-9580703fd066",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An engraving in wood or woodcut, especially one used in printing predating the Western tradition (14th c.)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d6a5d29-fdfa-4d6e-8bbd-a9305720833f",
                                                "sense_id": "34fd0cc6-08cf-3aca-979e-611a2da30d80",
                                                "text": "First he collected a number of witnesses, including many old prints of the Guhyasamāja Tantra itself and old xylograph prints of the Pradipodyotana from the monasteries of Drepung, Tashilhunpo, Riwo Dangchen, and Nartang."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36cd7034-32b5-3cc8-b982-9afdf2cd62e8",
                                        "entry_id": "4aae96f7-fde4-3ba2-8df7-9580703fd066",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A print taken from such an engraving."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed6838b1-93ba-43a0-b152-13d9a6549084",
                                                "sense_id": "36cd7034-32b5-3cc8-b982-9afdf2cd62e8",
                                                "text": "While Walter Gropius had had a reproduction of a xylograph from Lyonel Feininger reproduced on the Bauhaus movement's founding manifesto in 1919 – a symbolic image of a gothic cathedral that was comparatively traditional in both form […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e90fd12b-6b64-48bb-b616-7f84a72b3fda",
                                                "sense_id": "36cd7034-32b5-3cc8-b982-9afdf2cd62e8",
                                                "text": "The restoration process brought to light a sarira box containing an artifact that rewrote that history: the oldest xylograph in the world, reproduced in ink from woodblocks with characters carved in relief, was found inside the box from the second […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
